jotto -- the word game of Jotto===============================    jottoYou and the computer each secretly choose a common English word of fivedifferent letters, and take turns guessing.  Each wrong guess is answeredby the number of its letters that occur in the hidden word; the first toguess the other's word wins.  Type a bare carriage-return in place of aguess for a list of the computer's own answers so far.The computer plays from a built-in list of 1400-odd five-letter words(in GAMES/JOTTO); it whittles the list down as your answers rule wordsout, which is how it closes in on your word.G. L. Sicherman, 1990, translated to C from a UNIX f77 version that goesback through the original CDC FORTRAN IV to about 1975.  Free to use andmodify.  Originals in SRC/jotto/ORIG.